{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l2rmtiiw","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"group-15-elements-nitrogen-family","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pextra-pure-nsub2sub-can-be-obtained-by-heatingp-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-mjakfsxmxipzxqr5","content":"<p>Extra very pure N<sub>2</sub> can be obtained by heating</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"NH<sub>3</sub> with CuO"},{"identifier":"B","content":"NH<sub>4</sub>NO<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"(NH<sub>4</sub>)<sub>2</sub>CrO<sub>7</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Ba(N<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>Extra pure N<sub>2</sub> can be obtained by heating Ba(N<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>.</p>\n<h3>Explanation</h3>\n<h4>Thermal Decomposition of Barium Azide</h4>\n<p>Thermal decomposition of barium azide produces very pure nitrogen gas (N<sub>2</sub>).</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.568ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"26.832ex\" height=\"3.165ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1148 11859.7 1398.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Ba(N</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2433,-235.4) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2836.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(422,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"REL\" transform=\"translate(3939.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"undefined\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-2192\" transform=\"translate(288,0)\"></use><svg width=\"358\" height=\"180\" x=\"0\" y=\"160\" viewBox=\"89.5 160 358 180\"><use data-c=\"2190\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-2190\" transform=\"scale(0.88,1)\"></use></svg></g><g data-mml-node=\"mpadded\" transform=\"translate(0,683.2) scale(0.707)\"><g transform=\"translate(278,-200)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"></g></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\" transform=\"translate(5395.7,0)\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Ba</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6595.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6984.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D460\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D460\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(7453.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8064.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(9065.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(9565.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">N</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(633,-235.4) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(10601.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(10990.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(11470.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>This reaction yields pure nitrogen gas.</p>\n<h4>Decomposition of Ammonium Dichromate</h4>\n<p>Decomposition of ammonium dichromate ((NH<sub>4</sub>)<sub>2</sub>Cr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>7</sub>) produces chromium (III) oxide as impurities.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.568ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"40.846ex\" height=\"3.165ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1148 18053.9 1398.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(389,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">NH</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1233,-235.4) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2025.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(422,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2851.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Robo